{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqh314qvxgo","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Judge verdict APPROVE pluggable LLM backend seam and Claude provider","summary":"Single-attempt code review of impl /14 (commit 20d5bff) under feature pluggable-backend: APPROVED and auto-merged into orch/feature/pluggable-backend (feature head now 15a0a7c). Verified: (1) clean adapter interface — providers declare id/displayName/kind ('agentic-cli'|'api'); registry registerProvider validates shape and kind, throwing at registration; getActiveBackend reads overlay.config.backend and defaults to Claude. (2) CRITICAL callers-not-broken: lib/claude-cli.js is a pure re-export shim of resolveClaudeBin/loadEnvForClaude/needsShell from lib/llm-backend.js — confirmed IDENTITY-EQUAL at runtime (cc.resolveClaudeBin===lb.resolveClaudeBin etc.), and node --check passes on llm-backend.js, claude-cli.js, headless-drain.js, onboard-learn.js. (3) API ('api') kind is a clean THROWING stub (callApi/runJudgeLoop throw 'not implemented'), not half-built. (4) Scope clean — only the seam + Claude provider, 3 files (lib/llm-backend.js NEW, lib/claude-cli.js shim, test/llm-backend.test.js NEW); no drain-routing, config/hard-block, dashboard, real API backend, or Codex/Cursor providers leaked. (5) Tests 21/21 pass via node --test. getActiveBackend SOFT-falls-back to Claude on unknown provider id — judged ACCEPTABLE for the seam (a hard throw would brick every drain; the config/hard-block downstream task can tighten it), not a kick-back.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T20:16:07.495Z","vec":[-0.1358271688222885,-0.011511644348502159,-0.03532860800623894,-0.010660238564014435,0.0676942765712738,-0.041638534516096115,0.004202018957585096,0.07252305746078491,-0.04488203674554825,0.024823660030961037,0.014206494204699993,-0.000550475378986448,0.02120567113161087,-0.05078000947833061,-0.007202807813882828,0.06002216413617134,0.05329260230064392,0.0015158294700086117,-0.048419006168842316,0.014066573232412